WEBVTT

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.080
Shirou...

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.080
Welcome home.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.460
I'm back!

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.710
Sorry, I'm late.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.960
I got tied up at school.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.970
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.850
You were helping prepare for the School Festival, right?

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.430
Yeah.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.020
We only have a week.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.020
See you tomorrow!

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.560
We're at the most crucial stage of the preparations.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.110
All right.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.150
Can you get these documents over to Mr. Kuzuki for me?

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:52.980
Sure!

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:01.910
Listen up, everyone!

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.830
It's crunch time.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.960
We're almost there. We can do it!

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:25.450
Issei!

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.250
I finished fixing the supplies.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:33.380
Hey, sorry to dump that kind
of menial work on you, Emiya.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.340
It's okay. No worries at all.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.090
Looks like you have a lot going on here, too.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.840
Yeah. It's all the paperwork.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.220
Prepping for the School Festival planning,
and checking all the projects...

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.600
It's keeping us quite busy.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:53.350
I'm not part of the student council,

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.270
but let me know if there's anything I can do.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.690
I'll help.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.110
Yes. We appreciate the help.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:17.960
Coming in.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.260
Pardon me.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.220
Pardon me.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:26.390
What do you mean the Track and
Field Team's project is denied?

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.890
What's your explanation?
We need an explanation from you!

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.640
Chairman!

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.770
I think it's self-explanatory.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.280
What's this Beachside Grill Café?

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.110
There are lobsters, shrimp, raw oysters
and grilled Sazae shellfish on the menu!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.700
Are you insane? No way are we going to approve this!

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.040
Idiot!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.620
Come on!

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.130
In this day and age, no one will come
unless we do something like this!

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.210
Come back with something else!

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.970
I told you, Maki-no-ji.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.010
We should've gone with the standard squid.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.980
Kane, that's not what the problem is.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.890
Let's go back and come up with something else.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.650
I can't. Yukicchi, you're in charge now.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.230
Maki...

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.030
What in the world is this?

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.240
What do you mean?

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.120
These are the flowers the Archery
Club is using for decoration.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:38.460
But the student council never
received an application for this!

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:39.630
Denied!

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.590
You're kidding, right?

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.510
You mean we have to get approval
from the student council?

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:45.930
Oh, come on.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:51.010
Don't tell me you're canceling
after I lugged it all the way here.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:52.890
Hey!

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.430
Is that you, kid?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:58.100
Hey, you're working for a florist now?

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:01.480
Nope, someone needed my help,
so it's just a temporary side job.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:04.190
Wait, Emiya, you know him?

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.910
Well, yeah, kinda.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.870
So, what am I supposed to do with this?

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.080
Get rid of it!

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.950
You blockhead!

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.210
The rules need to be followed!

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.460
Cheapskate!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.880
I don't care!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.380
Ma'am?

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.220
Anger doesn't suit your pretty face.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.770
Listen!

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.770
Listen to me!

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.190
Well, I'm off.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:47.320
Okay.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.820
Do you think you'll be late again today?

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.580
Yeah. I'll probably be late.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.080
Do you have any requests for dinner tonight?

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.210
No.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.920
Please don't worry.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:21.270
You guys at the student council
work late every day. Are you okay?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.940
Issei, your eyes are glazing over.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:32.320
The list of tasks that we need to get done
to ensure a smooth process is endless.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.450
But just think, we'll be done
once we get through tonight.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.830
Thank you again for your support today.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.210
I'm counting on you for tomorrow.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.040
Got it. See you later, then!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.880
I'm so sick of eating sweet bread for dinner.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.130
Meat...

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.390
I want to eat meat.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.220
Meat, huh?

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.810
Yes.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.480
Meat would give us energy.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.940
If you're all still going to be here for a while,

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:10.030
I can make something to munch on if you want.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.160
Emiya's cooking...

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.780
But no! We can't ask you to do that!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.870
Wait! Did you say, "Emiya's...

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.120
Emiya's...

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.460
Emiya's cooking!

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.460
Food by Emiya!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.680
Okay then, I'll hurry and go.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.220
We'll be waiting!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.940
The chicken needs to be cut into bite-size pieces.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.870
Grate your garlic and ginger.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:02.710
Then mix the soy sauce, salt, pepper
and sake to make your marinade.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.920
Add your chicken to the marinade and massage it well.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.250
Leave it for about five minutes.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:18.430
Shake any excess marinade from your
chicken, and soak it in your egg wash.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.730
Mix the same amount of flour and corn starch,

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.900
and coat your egg-soaked chicken with it.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.570
Deep-fry it for about a minute and a half in oil

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.820
that's been heated to 160 to 180 degrees Celsius.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.790
Then cook the chicken with the
residual heat for about a minute.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:48.840
By doing this, you can lock in
the juicy taste of the chicken.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.340
Make a little crack and deep-fry it again.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.640
Repeat this process two or three more times,

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:59.970
and let the chicken cook all the way through.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:02.270
Lastly,

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:06.270
deep-fry it for 30 to 40 seconds
at a temperature of 200 Celsius.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:09.900
And it's done!

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.790
Karaage deep-fried chicken, huh?

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.540
We're grateful!

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.290
Thank you for the meal!

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:41.390
It's delicious.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.270
I wish there was an endless supply.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.980
So flavorful!

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:51.310
You mentioned meat, so I thought
Karaage deep-fried chicken would be good,

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:53.780
since it's easy to eat and tastes good even cold.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.240
That's our Emiya.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.360
So considerate.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:01.280
It's late, but thanks to this snack,
I think we can get through it!

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:02.200
Yes!

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:07.080
Wow, it's pitch-dark at this hour.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.080
I should get home, and...

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:30.020
Sorry!

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:31.690
I'm so late!

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.110
You must be starving.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.190
I'll make something right away!

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.530
No, no.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.030
I'm not really hun—

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.780
I don't think.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.370
I'll whip up something now!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.260
It's delicious, Shirou.
